============================================================================
1. The knot, and what the braid actually is
============================================================================
  trajectory braid  s1 s2^-1        -> SL(2,Z) matrix
[[2 1]
 [1 1]]
  trace 3, dilatation 2.618034, golden ratio squared 2.618034

  vineyard braid    (s2^-1 s1)^2   -> SL(2,Z) matrix
[[2 3]
 [3 5]]
  trace 7, dilatation 6.854102

  is the vineyard dilatation the square of the trajectory one? 0.00e+00
  topological entropy: trajectories 0.962424, vineyard 1.924847, ratio 2.000000

  m004, the once-punctured-torus bundle with monodromy [[2,1],[1,1]]:
    volume 2.029883, identified as [m004(0,0), 4_1(0,0)]

  So the same pseudo-Anosov map appears twice over: as the monodromy of
  the figure-eight knot fibration, and as the trajectory braid of the
  figure-eight orbit. The vineyard braid is its square, with exactly
  twice the entropy, and closes to that same knot.

